practice.a:
Multiply by the conjugate $\sqrt{4x+9}+3$:
\[
\frac{(\sqrt{4x+9}-3)(\sqrt{4x+9}+3)}{x(\sqrt{4x+9}+3)}
=\frac{4x+9-9}{x(\sqrt{4x+9}+3)}
=\frac{4x}{x(\sqrt{4x+9}+3)}
=\frac{4}{\sqrt{4x+9}+3}.
\]
Now let $x\to0$: $\displaystyle \frac{4}{\sqrt{9}+3}= \frac{4}{3+3}= \frac{4}{6}= \frac{2}{3}.$
